{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-158023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x+x{y}^{2}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x\\cdot (1+{y}^{2}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-158023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(1+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x"] ["math" "(x+x{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{x+x{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{1+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154678" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{x+1}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154678" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(\\frac{x}{x+1})\\cdot {y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{x+1}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154678" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-154678" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154678" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x+1)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x{y}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{x+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{x+1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}"] ["math" "{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{x+1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154678" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{x+1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot {y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-158027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1"] ["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\text{ }\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}"] ["math" "{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y{e}^{x}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\cdot y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-158022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1"] ["math" "y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}"] ["math" "{e}^{-x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y"] ["math" "{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}{x}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-158026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1"] ["math" "\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\,$ for $\\,|y|<1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y & =x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y=x+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-154367" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154367" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{arccos}⁡y=x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y=x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y=x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154367" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y=x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y & ={x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={x}^{3}+C"] ["math" "\\text{ }y={x}^{3}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}} \\\\ \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{2{y}^{3/2}}{3} & =\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+K \\\\ {y}^{3/2} & ={x}^{3/2}+C \\\\ \\sqrt{{y}^{3}} & =\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{3K}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-154373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C"] ["math" "\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=x+C"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C"] ["math" "y={x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "{y}^{3}=\\sqrt{x}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-158117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+K \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={x}^{3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3K.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-154361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y={x}^{3}+C"] ["math" "{y}^{2}={x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "{y}^{2}={x}^{3}+C"] ["math" "{y}^{3}=x+C"] ["math" "{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-154361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-158014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=K{e}^{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+K"] ["math" "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158013" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158013" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={sec}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158013" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-158013" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158013" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=K\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+K"] ["math" "y={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158013" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158012" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{3{y}^{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158012" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x}{3{y}^{2}} \\\\ 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}={x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158012" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-158012" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158012" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=(\\sqrt[3]{x}+C)^{2}"] ["math" "y=({x}^{2}+C)^{3}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{2}{3}x+C"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt[3]{2x+C}"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158012" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $|x|<1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-158016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=K{e}^{1/\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}+K"] ["math" "y={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-3850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x{e}^{-y}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-3850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x}{{e}^{y}} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{e}^{y}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-3850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-3850" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-3850" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+C"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-3850" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-14253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}+2{y}^{2}x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-14253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}+2{y}^{2}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}(1+2x) \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (1+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =x+{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{y}={x}^{2}+x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x+C}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-14253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-14253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-14253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{2x+C}"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x+C}"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x}+C"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}+x}+C"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+C}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-14253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x+C}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158010" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,{y}^{′}-y=0$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $|x|<1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158010" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,{y}^{′}-y & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158010" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-158010" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158010" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=K{e}^{1/\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-158010" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-79663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-2xy=3{x}^{2}y$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-79663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-2xy & =3{x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2xy & =3{x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}y+2xy \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(3{x}^{2}+2x)y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-79663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-79663" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-79663" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=K{e}^{3{x}^{2}+2x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{6x+2}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}+2x}}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-79663" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-79665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,{y}^{′}=1$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-79665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}{y}^{′} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2{y}^{1/2} & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n2{y}^{1/2}=\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{1/2} & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}+C \\\\ {y}^{1/2} & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2}+\\frac{C}{2} \\\\ y & ={(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2}+\\frac{C}{2})}^{2} \\\\ y & ={(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2}+K)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\frac{C}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-79665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-79665" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-79665" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{1}{9}\\,{x}^{3/2}+K"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{9}\\,{x}^{3}+K"] ["math" "y={(3{x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2}"] ["math" "y={(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2}+K)}^{2}"] ["math" "y={({x}^{3}+K)}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-79665" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2}+K)}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-79664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-{y}^{2}=6{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-79664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-{y}^{2} & =6{x}^{2}{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-{y}^{2} & =6{x}^{2}{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(6{x}^{2}+1){y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6{x}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6{x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (6{x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =2{x}^{3}+x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{y}=2{x}^{3}+x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+x+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-79664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb"} {"question" "q-79664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-79664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+x+C}"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{C}{2{x}^{3}+x}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-x}+C"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+C}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "q-79664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+x+C}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f721454bfe09f120531381d77d75d0deacc583c98cf29c36bedc0bb16ad8ab8"} {"question" "e-10849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $x,y \\geq 0,$ separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\sqrt{2xy}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/example-10849.json" "file_sha256" "bcf520050a87378e04d859edcc8db85e258dbbb1d43df8cfefe7f330c4526897"} {"question" "e-10849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{g(y)} \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} =  \\sqrt{2x} \\cdot  \\sqrt{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{y}} \\cdot \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} = \\sqrt{2x}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/example-10849.json" "file_sha256" "bcf520050a87378e04d859edcc8db85e258dbbb1d43df8cfefe7f330c4526897"} {"question" "e-10997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n    =\n    \\dfrac{x}{y}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/example-10997.json" "file_sha256" "b335c0fe38f222588aaae2888d5bfa22c4e7108ae113efc3af2f71261a999dec"} {"question" "e-10997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x}{y} \\\\ y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+K \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+2K \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C= 2K.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ny^2 = x^2 + C .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/example-10997.json" "file_sha256" "b335c0fe38f222588aaae2888d5bfa22c4e7108ae113efc3af2f71261a999dec"} {"question" "e-10832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y' = \\dfrac {x^2}{y}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/example-10832.json" "file_sha256" "f8fd12f51042371f834f9bbde315713093900153e983b9e60fc2eecb7d5f8998"} {"question" "e-10832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\ y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}y^2 = \\dfrac{1}{3}x^3 + C.\n$$\n\nWe can express the solution in the form $y = y(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+C \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+2C \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+2C} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+K}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K = 2C.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/example-10832.json" "file_sha256" "f8fd12f51042371f834f9bbde315713093900153e983b9e60fc2eecb7d5f8998"} {"question" "e-10833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y' + 2xy = 0$ for $y\\neq 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/example-10833.json" "file_sha256" "9e82b8f67fa194f48a1e8775f5847c138bb592feb33120741147b5c836ba16a4"} {"question" "e-10833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+2xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =-2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln \\vert y \\vert = -x^2 + C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y = y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-{x}^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K = e^C$  and $K > 0.$ \n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny = Ke^{-x^2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/example-10833.json" "file_sha256" "9e82b8f67fa194f48a1e8775f5847c138bb592feb33120741147b5c836ba16a4"}] "usage" {"q-154367" [] "e-10833" [] "q-154678" [] "e-10849" [] "e-10832" [] "e-10997" []} "basis" 1157 "retractions" [[17592186069006 :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation:\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{xy^{2}}{x + 1}$"] [17592186069006 :question/worked-solution "Factor the right-hand side as $\\frac{x}{x+1}y^2$. Where $y\\ne0$, divide both sides by $y^2$:\n$$\\frac1{y^2}\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{x}{x+1}.$$\nThis is the separated form for $x\\ne-1$. The solution $y=0$ must be considered separately because division by $y^2$ excludes it."] [17592186069006 :question/difficulty 17592186045465] [17592186069004 :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\sqrt{1 - y^{2}}$ for $\\mid y \\mid < 1$."] [17592186069004 :question/worked-solution "The condition $|y|<1$ permits division by $\\sqrt{1-y^2}$:\n$$\\frac{dy}{\\sqrt{1-y^2}}=dx.$$\nIntegrating gives $\\arcsin y=x+C$. An explicit form is $y=\\sin(x+C)$ on intervals where $-\\pi/2<x+C<\\pi/2$, which preserves $y'=\\sqrt{1-y^2}>0$."] [17592186069004 :question/difficulty 17592186045465] [17592186068372 :question/problem "Given that $x,y \\geq 0$, separate the variables in the following differential equation:\n\n$\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\sqrt{2xy}$"] [17592186068372 :question/worked-solution "A first-order differential equation is separable when it has the form $y'=h(x)g(y)$. Here, since $x,y\\ge0$,\n$$\\sqrt{2xy}=\\sqrt{2x}\\sqrt y.$$\nWhere $y>0$, division by $\\sqrt y$ gives the separated form\n$$\\frac1{\\sqrt y}\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\sqrt{2x}.$$\nThe division does not apply at $y=0$. The original equation also admits the equilibrium solution $y=0$, which must be considered separately."] [17592186068374 :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{x}{y}$."] [17592186068374 :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{x}{y} \\\\\ny\\frac{dy}{dx} &= x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int y\\frac{dy}{dx}dx &= \\int xdx \\\\\n\\int y\\frac{dy}{dx}dx &= \\int xdx \\\\\n\\int ydy &= \\int xdx \\\\\n\\frac{y^{2}}{2} &= \\frac{x^{2}}{2} + K \\\\\ny^{2} &= x^{2} + 2K \\\\\ny^{2} &= x^{2} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C= 2K$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ny^2 = x^2 + C\n$$"] [17592186068370 :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y' = \\dfrac {x^2}{y}$."] [17592186068370 :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{\\prime } &= \\frac{x^{2}}{y} \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{x^{2}}{y} \\\\\ny\\frac{dy}{dx} &= x^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int y\\frac{dy}{dx}dx &= \\int x^{2}dx \\\\\n\\int y\\frac{dy}{dx}dx &= \\int x^{2}dx \\\\\n\\int ydy &= \\int x^{2}dx \\\\\n\\frac{1}{2}y^{2} &= \\frac{1}{3}x^{3} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}y^2 = \\dfrac{1}{3}x^3 + C\n$$\n\nWe can express the solution in the form $y = y(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2}y^{2} &= \\frac{1}{3}x^{3} + C \\\\\ny^{2} &= \\frac{2}{3}x^{3} + 2C \\\\\ny &= \\pm  \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}x^{3} + 2C} \\\\\ny &= \\pm  \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}x^{3} + K}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K = 2C$."] [17592186068371 :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y' + 2xy = 0$ for $y\\neq 0$."] [17592186068371 :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{\\prime } + 2xy &= 0 \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx} + 2xy &= 0 \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= -2xy \\\\\n\\frac{1}{y} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} &= -2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int \\frac{1}{y} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}dx &= \\int (-2x)dx \\\\\n\\int \\frac{1}{y}dy &= -2\\int xdx \\\\\n\\ln \\mid y \\mid &= -x^{2} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln \\vert y \\vert = -x^2 + C\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y = y(x)$. By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\ln \\mid y \\mid &= -x^{2} + C \\\\\n\\mid y \\mid &= e^{-x^{2} + C} \\\\\n\\mid y \\mid &= e^{-x^{2}} \\cdot e^{C} \\\\\n\\mid y \\mid &= Ke^{-x^{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K = e^C$ and $K > 0$.\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny = Ke^{-x^2},\\qquad K\\ne0.\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186065819 17592186065820 17592186065821 17592186065822 17592186065823 17592186065831 17592186065832 17592186065833 17592186065834 17592186065835] "immutable_fields" [[17592186065818 :answer-field/correct] [17592186065818 :answer-field/id] [17592186065818 :answer-field/key] [17592186065818 :answer-field/type] [17592186065830 :answer-field/correct] [17592186065830 :answer-field/id] [17592186065830 :answer-field/key] [17592186065830 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
